{{Cleanup|date=March 2007}}
'''Funabashi Shrine''' (Funabashi Daijingū 船橋大神宮) is a [[Shinto]] shrine to the goddess [[Amaterasu ōmikami]], located in the city of [[Funabashi]] in [[Chiba prefecture]], [[Japan]].

==History==
By a company biography [[Emperor Keiko]] 40 years (Christian era [[110 age)]] ) [[Yamato Takeru]] I enshrine Amaterasu　here in an occasion of the east conquest and inform it that I begin though I prayed for the accomplishment of eastern country subjugation.it that inhabitants of here suffer from a drought and Yamato Takeru merges it and prays for offer prayers for rain in those days even if it has begun to rain.Originally "will wealth ratio God" (Dainichi God) who is sun god of a district is worshiped in the company; the outskirts ([[Tokyo Bay]]) in particular Of) [[fishermen]] Collected の faith,; but this whole area [[Ise-jingu Grand Shrine]] I am similar, and it is done oblation [[sacred kitchen]] and (Natsumi sacred kitchen.) I became) such as Funabashi sacred kitchen, and god Corporation who worshiped the Sun-Goddess who was an enshrined deity of [[Ise Shrine]]　Grand Shrine as the protection was erected, and god Corporation was enshrined together later by the company.Numinous company was enshrined together later by the company. It is considered that oohi God was identified with the Amaterasu ōmikami.

